> a(x:u32,y:u32)=(x+y) xor 1
> b(x:u32,y:u32)=((x^y)+2*(x&y)) xor 1
  note: "^" between integers, next to bitwise operators: read as power, not xor (bitwise exclusive or) (write xor or ** to say which)
  note: '^' is power; use 'xor' or '⊕' for exclusive or
> equiv a b
a and b differ at 65535 points of the sample, e.g. x=0, y=4294967294: 4294967295 vs 1
